SC,0006
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773098339
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, British Rail's internal inquiry into
OL,6, the Glasgow train crash has found
OL,7, evidence of human error.
OL,9,FThe inquiry found the signalling and
OL,10,Fbraking systems were working properly
OL,11,Fand did not contribute to the accident.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FScotrail said there was evidence of
OL,14,Fhuman error in the operation of the
OL,15,Ftrain bound for Springburn.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FThe driver of the other train and one
OL,18,Fpassenger were killed.
OL,19,F
OL,20,F
OL,21,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 09-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
