PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773098339
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Prescription charges are to rise by 20p
OL,6, to #2.80 on April 1, Health Secretary
OL,7, Mr Kenneth Clarke has announced.
OL,9,FThe increase, announced in a Commons
OL,10,Fwritten reply, will be the 11th rise in
OL,11,Fcharges since Mrs Thatcher came to
OL,12,Fpower in 1979, when the charge was 20p.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Clarke said it was an increase of
OL,15,F7.7 per cent which would provide the
OL,16,FNHS with an extra #10 million income.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FBut Labour spokesman Mr Robin Cook said
OL,19,Fthe increase was "a tax on the sick". A
OL,20,Fthird of drugs costed more on the NHS
OL,21,Fthan over the counter, he added.
OL,23,T]CFrom 09-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
